    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0385" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Riga</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-17T10:00:00+02:00">June 17, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 17—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. My 128, June 17, 2 a.m.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d371-f1"/> Am officially
                    informed Soviet troops are crossing border at many points and will occupy
                    Rezekne, Krustpils, Daugavpils,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d371-f2"/> Jelgava,<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d371-f3"/> Riga. It is expected they will enter capital this
                    afternoon. Government has resigned but it is expected Ulmanis will remain as
                    State President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
